  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_bf7b03cf38694772a9cf07c7c3291e97",
      "statement": "The service worker is registered by a classic script loaded from index.html via <script src=\"/register-sw.js?v=6\">; register-sw.js registers \"/sw.js?v=6\" from a one-shot window load listener, so registration happens after first paint and a registration failure only logs to console, leaving a working non-PWA page.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/web/index.html#L14-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b64331d379a01d2fc86987db469f530aa32712f96e22c4586a76fef73832e994:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/web/public/register-sw.js#L1-L11",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4d2bca57eb73109e81b43dbdbda0be8b19bf559d7f9b6d34462e15ba586053b5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_660fb2821e844e4fab2e162d71e8dd59",
      "statement": "The shell cache is a single versioned cache named mota-shell-v6 (SHELL_CACHE), and the cache version — not per-asset invalidation — is the deployment takeover mechanism: activating deletes every cache whose name differs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/web/public/sw.js#L1-L1",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9fcbef56cf0c15de8bb09377fd39513f3c172b02739c159e20869ded7592f608:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/web/public/sw.js#L34-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f6bca503ceab52e0727ab327fd73e45dec20b40bf1e9d654db2e31fe386ca2fa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3b7504f1f25948ddb924e5d3b0608c7d",
      "statement": "At install the worker fetches \"/\" with { cache: \"reload\" } and derives the shell asset list by regex-matching (?:src|href)=\"([^\"]+)\" over the HTML and keeping only root-relative paths, unioned (deduplicated via Set) with REQUIRED_SHELL; this picks up Vite's hashed /assets/* bundles from each deployment's own document without the worker knowing the hash scheme.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/web/public/sw.js#L10-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ef12747203193715267321786d51b128dcb8fe66d30e0e8d20198766e2d75f6c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/web/public/sw.js#L16-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7cf037fb81b6a21592889f350e0d20439d6c0ff512d52ab29a1107742fc0d894:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://dist/index.html#L19-L20",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4a787eda78e83ce0fbb6e03de2dde3b5537bd70bfaa1cd8b40dc3874dc0d3792:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6c15994e6ca44f3fb2f45ae092575059",
      "statement": "REQUIRED_SHELL hard-codes the five assets the HTML does not self-describe — /manifest.webmanifest, /pwa-icon-192.png, /pwa-icon-512.png, /pwa-icon.svg, and /register-sw.js?v=6 — while sw.js itself is deliberately absent because the browser's service-worker update path fetches the worker file independently.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/web/public/register-sw.js#L5-L5",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5fcad57f67b45f6a5549a18aff969d8730cc7d2141a9fc674ffdfe4852ee8272:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/web/public/sw.js#L1-L8",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:92dec35befaaf19433fefd3dad62da7d5791c09c2148ca8cfbbf70a68ba6d3a7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_eb3fc55271ac4d6a935cac3b975bbde1",
      "statement": "A non-OK root response aborts installation: the install handler throws before any cache.put, and event.waitUntil propagates the rejection so the browser keeps the previous worker in control; cache.addAll has the same all-or-nothing semantics for the asset list, so a broken or missing asset also aborts the install rather than caching a half-populated shell.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/web/public/sw.js#L16-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7cf037fb81b6a21592889f350e0d20439d6c0ff512d52ab29a1107742fc0d894:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7d2f9826a3904fc989ba7edb73f5686b",
      "statement": "self.skipWaiting() runs inside install's waitUntil after the cache is fully populated, and activate then calls self.clients.claim(), so a new version takes control of existing clients in one page-load cycle instead of waiting for tabs to close.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/web/public/sw.js#L29-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3b1ef899324804b7ae4c9dd2d1d3ab5a69f0949b2dd504ca85533611f6b93b1b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/web/public/sw.js#L34-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f6bca503ceab52e0727ab327fd73e45dec20b40bf1e9d654db2e31fe386ca2fa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b7b8b5711870412faa88d1f3edb0bc61",
      "statement": "The fetch handler bails out without responding for any request that is non-GET, cross-origin, or whose pathname starts with /api/; the service worker therefore never serves or caches /api/* — stated as a hard rule in AGENTS.md — so transit data, settings sync, and auth probes always hit the server or fail, and OpenStreetMap map tiles (cross-origin) pass through untouched.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://AGENTS.md#L74-L74",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bae314e15c091d94efd1df96e6cd043ba3602ef94e4f3b154f09248517ac8ed6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/web/public/sw.js#L48-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:71072482cd61d911421b7d3c003f348da25bc3ef3b895b0353109ee8fd73b643:"
        },
        {
