    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fcf288ad519040da89cdda694ded44ec",
      "statement": "Navigations (request.mode === \"navigate\") are network-first: a successful response is cached under the literal key \"/\" regardless of the requested URL, and on network failure the handler serves caches.match(\"/\") as the fallback, rethrowing the original error only if no cached shell exists — so offline deep links still boot the app via the root document.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/web/public/sw.js#L59-L78",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e73622b7ca03bb5171b8102b1a5206bfbdb1e6cb7ce2d0bf61a9ef1633c78f45:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1f4581dfcba64fd18171639d661db2ca",
      "statement": "Non-navigation same-origin GET requests use a cache-first strategy: caches.match first, and on a miss the network response is written into SHELL_CACHE if OK; the branch has no offline fallback, so only navigations and already-cached assets work offline.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/web/public/sw.js#L80-L92",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:169f19c9f4e9a9cdcc0c1bd6c151d4ed489cbcd9bc75c439ff034be8ca61c554:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_00d2a0f1985d4f6699a5d7a594da0df1",
      "statement": "manifest.webmanifest declares id, start_url, and scope all \"/\", display \"standalone\", lang \"ko-KR\", theme_color #0b0b0b, background_color #f7f7f3, and four icons (192x192 PNG any, 512x512 PNG any, the same 512x512 PNG maskable, and /pwa-icon.svg any); it deliberately omits orientation because a manifest orientation value overrides the OS rotation lock (Chromium issue 40880635).",
      "evidence": [
